# Datasets. The leading slash anchors this to the repository root: a bare
# "data/" would also match src/radon/data/, silently excluding the data-loading
# package from every commit.
#
# NOTE: /data/ was already committed in this repository's history, so this rule
# only prevents *new* dataset files from being added; it does not untrack the
# existing ones. Consider `git rm --cached -r data/` before publishing: MNIST
# and NSL-KDD are both freely downloadable and add ~50 MB to every clone.
/data/

